    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that the matter described above is lawful within the meaning of section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reasons:\r\n\r\nThe side extension being 2.3m wide and 2.8m deep, with a flat roof height of 3m, that, along with the existing two-storey rear extension adds a total volume of 59.32m3 to the original dwellinghouse, as shown on the plans received on the 21st June 2004 constitutes permitted development as defined by Schedule 2, Part 1, Class A of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995 (as amended) and therefore does not require planning permission.\r\n"
